 41
12.0
 71
1
  3
SYSTEM A - NOTES (REV 1)\PRev 1: stair well and elevator shaft NOT roofed (openings, hatched); single roof plane, TOS = 3.45 + 0.06 x (35.87 - y): north edge 3.45 m, south edge y 15.57 4.67 m.\POpenings: trimmers IPE200 at N and S edges spanning F3-F
  3
4 rafters (4.05 m); F3/F4 rafters on the shaft walls form the E/W edges; upstand + flashing all sides, no purlin crosses an opening.\PFrames: rigid mono-pitch portals on every N-S column line, pinned bases, haunched bolted end-plate knees (M20 8.8).\
  3
PRafters: IPE300 S275 (F2 13.4+6.0 m; F5/F6 9.2 propped + 6.5 m), IPE240 elsewhere (bays <= 6.4 m).\PColumns: HEA200 (F2, F5, F6), HEA160 (other frames, eave posts). Haunches 1.0-1.3 m cut from rafter section.\PEaves beams IPE200; transfer eave girde
  3
r IPE300 on K21-K22-K23 carries F5/F6 south rafter ends (no column below).\PPurlins Z200x2.0 S350GD @ 1.5 m, sleeved, 1 row sag bars/bay. Girts Z150x1.5 @ 1.5 m.\PStability: N-S portal action; E-W vertical X bracing rods M20 in bays K6-K5, K2-K4, K25
  3
-K26, K22-K23 + roof X CHS 76.3x3.2 in bays 68.0-72.1, 81.85-87.2, 92.5-95.55 and one panel 77.8-81.85 between the openings.\PBases: 300x400x20 plate on 30-50 mm non-shrink grout, 4 x M20 chemical anchors hef 160-180 in solid zone over column head; u
  3
plift 25-35 kN, shear 25-45 kN/base.\PLoads: G 0.45, Q 0.60, qp 1.30 kN/m2, net uplift -1.0 to -1.3 (edge -3.3) kN/m2.\PSteel (Rev 1): primary 13.3 t = 27 kg/m2 of footprint (484 m2); incl. purlins/girts approx. 16.3 t = 34 kg/m2 (37 kg/m2 of the 444
  1
 m2 roofed).
