NOTES - SYSTEM B (REV 1)\PRoof: ONE plane, 6% falling N. TOS(y) = 4.52 + 0.06 x (35.87 - y): TOS 4.52 m at N edge, 5.74 m at S edge; bottom chord underside 3.00 m (N) to 4.22 m (S).\PTrusses: parallel-chord Warren, depth 1.40 m c/c. T1 19.3 m (x 68.0
  3
/72.1/77.8), T2 15.6 m (x 81.8/87.2/92.5/95.5).\PChords SHS 120x120x5 all trusses; diagonals SHS 70x70x4 (S275J2H hot-finished, shop-welded K-joints, T1 site splice M20 8.8).\POpenings: stair x 77.89-81.79 / y 29.37-35.37 and elevator x 77.89-81.99 /
  3
 y 20.17-24.16 not roofed; trimmers SHS 100x100x4 on N+S edges, trusses x 77.8 / 81.8 on E/W edges; upstand + flashing; no purlin, tie or bracing crosses them.\PPosts SHS 150x150x5 on 19 of 27 columns, pinned bases: 300x300x20 plate, 40 mm grout, 4 M
  3
20 resin anchors 300 mm into column head.\PPurlins Z200x2.0 S350GD @ 1.5 m, sleeved. Eave girder IPE 330 (y 20.07, K21-K23), header IPE 200 at re-entrant corner.\PBracing: L70x70x6 tension-only X in 8 wall bays + 3 roof bays (top chord level); eave s
  3
truts SHS 100x100x4; BC ties SHS 60x60x4.\PLoads: g 0.50 (0.30 uplift), q 0.60, qp 1.32 kN/m2; ULS 1.58 kN/m2 down / 1.68 kN/m2 up. Post uplift ~88 kN governs anchors.\PSteel: ~14.9 t = ~33 kg/m2 over 446 m2 roofed (31 kg/m2 of 486 m2 footprint) + gi
  1
rts ~1.0 t.
