1
  3
SYSTEM C NOTES - REV 1\PSections S275: HEA 160 columns (27); IPE 330 E-W primaries on cap plates; IPE 270 N-S rafters and edge beams (fin plates, bottom flanges flush); Z200x2.0 S350 purlins and girts @ 1.5 m; wall bracing 2L 70x7 crossed tension-onl
  3
y; roof bracing M20 rods.\PSingle roof plane 6% falling north: top of steel TOS = 3.28 + 0.06 x (35.87 - y). Cap-plate top = TOS - 0.27: 3.00 (y 35.7) / 3.03 (35.2) / 3.39 (29.3) / 3.56 (26.4) / 3.68 (24.5) / 3.84 (21.8) / 3.94 (20.1) / 4.19 (15.9) m
  3
. Rafters frame into primary webs with fin plates, bottom flanges flush, ends cut at 3.4 deg - no seats or packs; primary top = TOS + 0.06.\POpenings: stair well and elevator shaft not roofed; long edges = rafters x 77.8 / 81.8, stair south edge = y 
  3
29.3 primary, stair north edge = trimmer T1 (y 35.17, K7 to rafter 81.8, replaces skewed K7-K3 beam), elevator north edge = trimmer T2 (y 24.16), south edge = eave beam y 20.07. 150 mm upstand + flashing all sides, cricket on the uphill (south) side 
  3
of the stair opening. Roof truss jogs south of the stair opening (X in panel K10-K11-K17-K16).\PWeight: hot-rolled incl. plates 16.7 t; total with purlins, girts, bracing, upstands 20.5 t = 42 kg/m2 of footprint (486 m2) = 46 kg/m2 of roofed area (44
  3
6 m2).\PWall bracing bays (door-free, to confirm): E-W B1 K1-K2, B2 K5-K7, B3 K22-K23, B4 K25-K26; N-S B5 K15-K19, B6 K14-K18, B7 K20-K27. Roof-plane X strip 3.2 m around the perimeter.\PBases: 300x400x20 plate, 4 M20 resin anchors hef 170-200 mm in 
  1
solid column-head zone only, 40 mm grout. Design uplift up to 70 kN, shear 15 kN at braced-bay columns.
